{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the veils.</b> Like a large veil [similarly]." "<b>And the fine linens.</b> Like 'she makes fine linen' (Proverbs 31:24)." "<b>And the turbans.</b> On the head." "<b>And the shawls.</b> Ṭallit in the language of Ishmael. The general principle is that all of these are garments and they change according to the custom of the places."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:13.784725026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}